  "notes": "The Shaytan and the angels are never drawn; his promise (48:6-15) is not glossed, and As-Sa'di's report of his appearance is not used. The hypocrites' saying (49:8-10) is framed «يقولونه احتقارا لهم». Light for «ومن يتوكل على الله». Al-Muyassar's «توبة نصوحًا» (Quran wording) not used. STAGING v4: c1 (48) stays ambient: the Shaytan's promise and his turning back when the two armies met at Badr (the Shaytan, the angels and the battle are never drawn); a geometric plate only for Allah's severe punishment (48:34, after the Shaytan's words). c2 (49): a town by day. Three faceless figures (a neutral people group of three: the hypocrites and those with doubt in their hearts, As-Sa'di: weak in faith) walk in from the right and speak on 49:2 and again on 49:8; on the demonstrative 49:9 they point at three believers standing on the left (Al-Muyassar: they see the Muslims; As-Sa'di: said of the believers) and shake their heads on 49:10 (contempt, framed by As-Sa'di's gloss). Only the speakers gesture; the believers do nothing. On the general statement of reliance (49:11-14) the camera holds on the believers, with no gesture (it is a general conditional); a seal plate for trusting His promise (49:12, Al-Muyassar's gloss), then a geometric plate on the Name for Mighty and Wise (49:16). The place is not named by the tafsirs, so a plain town is used; no army, no enemy and no battle are drawn."
